.TH TABLEPRO 1 2026-04-26 "TablePro 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tablepro \- work with your databases
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tablepro
.RI [ OPTION ...]
.RI [ FILE ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
TablePro connects to PostgreSQL, MySQL, SQLite, DuckDB, SQL Server, ClickHouse,
Cassandra, ScyllaDB and Redis.
It browses tables, edits rows in place, runs SQL with syntax highlighting,
and reaches servers behind an SSH bastion through the system OpenSSH client.
.PP
Each
.I FILE
is a SQLite or DuckDB database, opened in its own window.
A running TablePro opens the files itself and the new launch exits.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-new\-window
Open a new window, in the running TablePro when there is one.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the options and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help\-all
Show every option, including the GApplication ones, and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Which messages are logged to standard error, as a tracing filter such as
.BR info " or " tablepro=debug .
.TP
.B TABLEPRO_LOG_FORMAT
.B json
logs one JSON object per line.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/tablepro/connections.json
The saved connections: hosts, ports, user names and SSH settings.
Passwords are not in it; they are in the Secret Service keyring.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/tablepro/column_widths.json
.TQ
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/tablepro/filter_settings.json
Column widths and filters, kept per table.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/tablepro/history.db
The query history and the saved queries, in a SQLite database.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/tablepro/workspaces/
The tabs of each connection, and which connections were open at the last quit.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/tablepro/drafts/
The text of each SQL editor tab.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/tablepro/crashes/
A report of each crash.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/app/app.tablepro.TablePro/ssh/
The control sockets of the open SSH tunnels.
.PP
When unset,
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is
.IR ~/.config ,
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
is
.I ~/.local/state
and
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
is
.IR ~/.local/share .
Preferences are kept in GSettings, under the schema
.BR app.tablepro.TablePro .
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at https://github.com/TableProApp/TablePro/issues.
Include the text that Copy Text puts on the clipboard in
About TablePro > Troubleshooting > Debugging Information.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh (1),
.BR ssh_config (5),
.BR gsettings (1)
.PP
https://docs.tablepro.app
